    intro: "So God created man in his own image, in the image of God he created him; male and female he created them. Husbands, love your wives, as Christ loved the church and gave himself up for her. Live with your wives in an understanding way, showing honour to the woman as the weaker vessel, since they are heirs with you of the grace of life.",
    context: "In many ancient societies, women had little protection. Jesus honoured women as disciples, defended them from condemnation, and appeared first to women after the resurrection. Paul wrote about mutual love and respect. Yet throughout history, Scripture has sometimes been misused to justify abuse or silence victims. Today, many women and girls experience domestic violence, sexual assault, harassment, forced or early marriage, female genital cutting, trafficking, economic abuse and discrimination, often with little help.",
